From 9eb681bef60b3b10be3a4fa1a2c13b3e876196d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bowen Wang <wangbowen1001@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 23:18:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(bench): count requests the server aborts in-stream as
 failed

A server that fails a request after sending the 200 header reports it inside the stream: an OpenAI-style error event, or finish_reason.type == "abort" on the native endpoint. The chat and native streaming paths skipped that event and recorded a completed request with the requested output length, so a run against a server that sheds load (for example SGLANG_REQ_WAITING_TIMEOUT) reported completed requests and output tokens that were never produced. The completions path already failed such a request, with a KeyError traceback as the message. All three now record a failed request carrying the server's message.
---
 python/sglang/benchmark/serving.py            |  59 +++++++--
 .../bench/test_bench_serving_stream_error.py  | 119 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 166 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 test/registered/unit/bench/test_bench_serving_stream_error.py

diff --git a/python/sglang/benchmark/serving.py b/python/sglang/benchmark/serving.py
